<%#
  About me — Depth Charge restyle (Task 8). The .bg-waves-2 photo background
  is gone now that the black-hole canvas sits behind every section. All
  three real beats (profile intro, adventure, Thai PBS documentary) are
  kept — the brief only calls out paragraph/embed styling, not trimming the
  content — stacked single-column instead of the old two-column rows, each
  photo/video framed the same way via .framed-media.
%>
<section id="about-me" class="sec justify-content-start"
         data-sec data-role="about" data-ax="0.66" data-label="About">
  <div class="section-inner" style="max-width: 600px;">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">◆ About Me</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading mb-4">About me.</h2>

    <div class="framed-media mb-4">
      <%= image_tag "lb-portfolio.jpeg", alt: "Louis web developer", class: "w-100" %>
    </div>
    <p class="text-body-soft mb-4" style="font-size: 16.5px;">Mixed British-Thai developer based in Thailand, which I now call home after growing up across multiple countries. Fluent in English and Thai, with a long-standing love of tech 🤓 that naturally led into full‑stack development. Also an independent trader and financial analyst, combining technical charting with a structured, risk‑first approach to the markets 📊.</p>

    <div class="framed-media mb-4">
      <%= image_tag "mt-cook-ta.jpg", alt: "Louis web developer", class: "w-100" %>
    </div>
    <p class="text-body-soft mb-4" style="font-size: 16.5px;">Beyond code and charts, staying active is a big part of life - lifting, kitesurfing, running, and hiking - and that love of adventure took me all the way through New Zealand’s 3,000 km Te Araroa thru‑hike, which I completed over four months in 2024/2025 🚀.</p>

    <div class="framed-media mb-3">
      <iframe height="350" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/X427QTamroE?si=cIjvoF9l_rCW2GHn" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" class="w-100" allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>
    <h3 class="project-card-title mb-2">Thai PBS - 2C Climate Change Documentary Series (2019): Episode 4</h3>
    <p class="text-body-soft" style="font-size: 16.5px;">Served as a TV presenter for a five‑episode climate change documentary along the Gulf of Thailand, covering the coastlines of Thailand, Cambodia, and Vietnam. The series explores key environmental challenges across Southeast Asia and still airs on Thai national TV.</p>
  </div>
</section>
